bility":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0035074054610156214,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":15.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.021230736437824447,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":64.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.01268,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":8.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.444,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":44.4,"pf":[],"description_full":"Pinnacle Financial Partners, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for Pinnacle Bank that provides various banking products and services to individuals, businesses, and professional entities in the United States. It accepts various deposits, including savings, noninterest-bearing and interest-bearing checking, money market, and certificate of deposit accounts; and provides treasury management services, such as online wire origination, enhanced ACH origination, positive pay, zero balance and sweep accounts, automated bill pay services, electronic receivables processing, lockbox processing, and merchant card acceptance services, small business and commercial credit cards corporate purchasing cards, and virtual accounting/deposit escrow solutions. The company also offers equipment and working capital loans; commercial real estate loans, such as investment properties and business loan; secured and unsecured loans comprising installment and term, lines of credit, and residential first mortgage, as well as home equity loans and home equity lines of credit; and credit cards for consumers and businesses. In addition, the company provides investment products; brokerage and investment advisory programs; and fiduciary and investment services, including personal trust, investment management, estate administration, endowments, foundations, individual retirement accounts, escrow services, and custody. Further, it offers insurance agency services in the property and casualty area; investment, merger and acquisition advisory services, private debt, equity and mezzanine placement services, and other middle-market advisory services; and other banking services, including telephone and online banking, mobile banking, debit cards, direct deposit and remote deposit capture, mobile deposit option, automated teller machine, and cash management services. Pinnacle Financial Partners, Inc. was incorporated in 2000 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin S. Blair | President, CEO & Director | Age 54","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $240K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $79K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Pinnacle Financial Partners, In is a large-cap financial services business with a $15.3B market cap on $2.1B of annual revenue.","The business throws off $679M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 33 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.18\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Shareholder yield is only 0.4%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $17.4M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-17385573.31},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Fulcrum Asset Management LLP Buys 7,249 Shares of Pinnacle Financial Partners, Inc. $PNFP","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/fulcrum-asset-management-llp-buys-7249-shares-of-pinnacle-financial-partners-inc-pnfp.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794559267.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.941,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Behavioral Patterns of PNFP and Institutional Flows","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/141/Behavioral_Patterns_of_PNFP_and_Institutional_Flows_111326022602_1794554762.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794554762.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"3 Financial Stocks With Rising Rate Exposure In U.S. Banks And Asset Management","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-apo/apollo-global-management/news/3-financial-stocks-with-rising-rate-exposure-in-us-banks-and"